30,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The data is damning. The apron outside the civic hall has been patched three times. The eastern avenue trees are dead.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Only two firms can handle the earth-moving, and both flagged slippage risk. The southern ground can be hoarded, but the centre cannot.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Planted ground costs triple to maintain. The habitat fund only pays for planting, not surfacing. The gap is widening.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The roll is down to seven. We buy in specialist care, but volunteers cover weekends. It’s a fragile mix.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"Drainage callouts doubled. Heat readings are high. People cross on firm ground, avoiding the soft margins.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, the habitat fund terms are a trap. It pays for planting, but not the hard surfaces that actually last.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the slippage risk is real. We cannot dig in the centre. We must phase from the south.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, if we can't dig in the centre, we can't do a full plaza. The costs for planting are too high.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the volunteer groups are helpful, but they can't replace the lost staff. We need a plan that doesn't need constant expert care.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, the people avoid the soft margins. A wetland or dense woodland will be ignored or damaged.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"The past shows us that soft, planted areas fail without constant, expensive care. Hard surfaces last, but they are expensive to build.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,We must avoid the centre. The southern phasing is the only safe route. This limits our options significantly.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,The upkeep ledger is clear. Planted ground is a financial black hole. We need something that doesn't cost triple to maintain.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"With only seven staff, we cannot manage a complex ecosystem. We need a simple, robust plan.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,The drainage data confirms the ground is saturated. Adding more water features is a mistake. We need firm ground.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am leaning towards a plan that respects the past failures. No more dead trees.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I am leaning towards a plan that respects the ground. No digging in the centre.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,I am leaning towards a plan that respects the budget. No triple-cost maintenance.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I am leaning towards a plan that respects the staff. No complex care.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I am leaning towards a plan that respects the users. Firm ground, not soft margins.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
