60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidates are A: Market Plaza, B: Woodland Walk, C: Wetland Restoration, D: Sports Terraces.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, A and D are hard surfaces. B and C are soft. The ground data favors A or D.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, A and D are hard surfaces. The upkeep ledger favors A or D. B and C are too expensive.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, A and D are simpler to maintain. B and C require specialist care we don't have.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, A and D provide firm ground. B and C are soft margins people avoid.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,A is a plaza. D is sports. Both are hard. But A has stall infrastructure. D has changing facilities.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,A is in the centre. D is on the south. The phasing notes say the south can be hoarded. The centre cannot.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mio,,A is a plaza. D is sports. Both are hard. But A has utility connections. D has stepped seating.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,A is a plaza. D is sports. Both are hard. But A has weekend markets. D has youth leagues.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,A is a plaza. D is sports. Both are hard. But A is for events. D is for daily use.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, if the centre can't be hoarded, A is risky. D is on the south, which can be phased.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, exactly. D is the only option that fits the phasing constraints. A is too central.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, D is hard surface. The upkeep is lower. A is also hard, but the utility connections might add cost.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, D has volunteer groups already lining the youth league grounds. A has no existing volunteer base.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, D is for daily use. The timed counts show people crossing for the tram. D provides a clear path.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"D is the logical choice. It fits the phasing, the budget, the staffing, and the usage.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,D is the only option that respects the ground. I vote for D.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mio,,D is the only option that respects the budget. I vote for D.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Asuka,,D is the only option that respects the staff. I vote for D.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,D is the only option that respects the users. I vote for D.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
